> **TieredKV** is a research simulator and model-integrated cache policy for a two-tier KV hierarchy (1024-token VRAM working set + 2048-token hypothetical STT-RAM victim cache). It studies whether retaining evicted tokens can recover accuracy. The STT-RAM tier and its bandwidth, latency, and energy are **analytical**: tensors still reside in GPU memory during real-model evaluation. Reported GPU allocation and measured latency therefore describe this Python/GPU prototype, not an STT-RAM device. Dropped tokens are discarded, not offloaded.

